From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:34:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: brcmfmac: don't cancel the bus reset work before it
 exists

drvr->bus_reset is initialised in brcmf_bus_started(), after the
firmware is up. When the firmware fails to start, the PCIe setup path
unbinds the device, and brcmf_pcie_remove() calls
brcmf_bus_cancel_reset_work(), which runs cancel_work_sync() on a work
item that was never initialised and trips the check in __flush_work():

  WARNING: kernel/workqueue.c:4409 at __flush_work+0x27c/0x2a4
  Call trace:
   __flush_work+0x27c/0x2a4 (P)
   __cancel_work_sync+0xbc/0x1dc
   cancel_work_sync+0x14/0x24
   brcmf_bus_cancel_reset_work+0x38/0x50 [brcmfmac]
   brcmf_pcie_remove+0x6c/0x168 [brcmfmac]
   pci_device_remove+0x48/0xdc
   device_release_driver_internal+0x16c/0x27c
   device_release_driver+0x18/0x24
   brcmf_pcie_setup+0x434/0xa4c [brcmfmac]

brcmf_bus_schedule_reset() already treats a NULL work function as "not
armable yet". Use the same test before cancelling: there is nothing to
cancel when the work was never set up.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c
index 92ec269f4..1e8a0b183 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c
@@ -1186,7 +1186,8 @@ void brcmf_bus_cancel_reset_work(struct brcmf_bus *bus_if)
 {
 	mutex_lock(&bus_if->bus_reset_lock);
 	bus_if->removing = true;
-	if (bus_if->drvr)
+	/* bus_reset is only initialised once the bus has started */
+	if (bus_if->drvr && bus_if->drvr->bus_reset.func)
 		cancel_work_sync(&bus_if->drvr->bus_reset);
 	mutex_unlock(&bus_if->bus_reset_lock);
 }
